      "writtenOn": "2026-07-03T14:54:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using aom_memset16() results in integer sanitizer runtime error as reported in the sanitizer build \u003chttps://build.aomedia.org/jenkins/job/libaom__per_commit-unit_test-sanitizers/31675/GTEST_SHARD_INDEX\u003d0,sanitizer\u003dinteger/consoleFull\u003e. This is because the buffer being initialized is of type int16_t and using aom_memset16() causes an implicit signed-to-unsigned conversion when a negative value is passed. Thus we have reverted to using aom_memset_int16() to avoid the sanitizer failure. The fix is available in https://aomedia-review.googlesource.com/c/aom/+/214741. Please review. \n\nAs the function aom_memset16() stores the value through a uint16_t * we see that the function prototype should be more accurately expressed as follows:\n\nvoid *aom_memset16(void *dest, uint16_t val, size_t length)",
      "parentUuid": "ac88faa4_c84db0af",
